  "id": "COMPOUND:7796 - PROTEIN:5805",
  "verbalization": "Spaglumic acid is implicated in the pathogenesis of SCCH-26 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Spaglumic acid acts as a target for multiple compounds, including beta-Cuprenene and Zanthomuurolanine, which in turn target SCCH-26. These relationships are supported by a consistent score across different paths, indicating a plausible biological link. The mechanism of action appears to involve the inhibition of SCCH-26 through the targeting of downstream molecules, which may exert a cytotoxic effect on the cell line. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Spaglumic acid in modulating the activity of these compounds, which could be relevant in the development of therapeutic strategies targeting SCCH-26. The evidence is consistent and supports a mechanistic relationship, though further validation through experimental studies would be necessary to confirm the exact role of Spaglumic acid in this context.",
